        <content type="html" xml:base="/projects/med-ethics/">&lt;h3 id=&quot;the-malfunction&quot;&gt;The malfunction&lt;&#x2F;h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On december 6th the &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;med-ethics.drismir.ca&quot;&gt;UBC Medical Ethics&lt;&#x2F;a&gt; club website had a
catastrophic UI failure.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;&#x2F;projects&#x2F;med-ethics&#x2F;ui_fail.png&quot; alt=&quot;ui_failure&quot; &#x2F;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As you can see the the leaderboard header is obscured by the beaker png. The leaderboard header and
beaker png are both performance critical, I needed to quickly resolve this conflict before
our malfunctioning UI caused undue stress for our users.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;the-solution&quot;&gt;The solution&lt;&#x2F;h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fortunately me and @ny4h1c were able to engineer an elegant and maintainable solution.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;&#x2F;projects&#x2F;med-ethics&#x2F;ui_fix.png&quot; alt=&quot;ui_fix&quot; &#x2F;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As you can see we managed to keep both the leaderboard header and beaker png online with
minimal disruption to our loyal users. This was achieved with the following CSS rules:&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
